cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Proactive Feasibility Scheduler: Simulation-Driven GPU Job
  Scheduling with ML-Based Wait-Time Prediction
message: >-
  If you use this software, its results, or its methodology in
  your work, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Rakshit
    family-names: Rameshbabu
    email: rakshitoffl@gmail.com
    # affiliation: "<add your institution here>"
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/rakshit-737/proactive-feasibility-scheduler
url: >-
  https://github.com/rakshit-737/proactive-feasibility-scheduler
abstract: >-
  A simulation-driven study of proactive GPU-cluster job scheduling that uses a
  machine-learning wait-time predictor to reorder the queue. The repository
  contains a 30-phase research pipeline: discrete-time cluster simulation,
  wait-time regression modelling, a five-scheduler benchmark (FIFO, SJF,
  Priority, Proactive, and a neural-network scheduler), ablation and SHAP
  explainability, fairness and starvation analysis, an EASY-backfill baseline
  with a tunable fairness budget, uncertainty-aware scheduling, scaling and
  concept-drift studies, real-trace validation on Parallel Workloads Archive
  traces (LANL CM-5, SDSC SP2), ROI analysis, and a one-command
  reproducibility kit.
keywords:
  - job scheduling
  - GPU cluster
  - high-performance computing
  - machine learning
  - wait-time prediction
  - backfilling
  - reproducible research
  - queue optimization
license: MIT
